  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "By default, a user can always grab a pickup with the other hand while holding it with one hand, to switch hands. \nThis becomes a problem e.g. when you create a controller that needs to be held in one hand and operated with the other hand, sudden unwanted hand switches can occur, you cannot make the user press \"grab\" with the other hand in reach of that pickup. This also becomes a problem e.g. if you want to track something while the pickup is held, because the OnDrop+OnPickup event will fire while still holding it, even though it was never dropped.\nWe need the ability to disable hand switching on a pickup without dropping the pickup first. \nUnfortunately, disabling the \"pickupable\" property in OnPickup does not already enable this behavior. I would at least expect that doing that leads to the wanted result of disallowing a hand switch.",
